see still fake readings but in backend its working 

Your backend is STILL forwarding the pretty text lines to React.

Console proves it.

React receives:

LIVE SENSOR: HR: 77 BPM
instead of ONLY:

{"heartRate":77,"spo2":98,"temperature":36.5,"respiration":14}
So your server.cjs filter is NOT applied correctly yet.

This is the REAL final fix.

OPEN
server/server.cjs
FIND THIS ENTIRE BLOCK
You probably still have something like:

parser.on("data", (line) => {

    console.log("ESP32:", line);

    wss.clients.forEach((client) => {
        if (client.readyState === 1) {
            client.send(line);
        }
    });

});
DELETE IT
Replace with THIS EXACT CODE:

parser.on("data", (line) => {

    console.log("ESP32:", line);

    // ONLY SEND JSON LINES
    if (line.trim().startsWith("{")) {

        wss.clients.forEach((client) => {

            if (client.readyState === 1) {
                client.send(line);
            }

        });

    }

});
WHY THIS FIXES IT
Your ESP32 sends BOTH:

HR: 77 BPM
AND:

{"heartRate":77,"spo2":98,"temperature":36.5,"respiration":14}
Now server forwards ONLY lines starting with:

{
So React receives only valid JSON.

No parse errors.

No fake readings.

No browser emotional collapse.

THEN RESTART EVERYTHING
STOP ALL TERMINALS
CTRL + C

TERMINAL 1
node server/server.cjs
TERMINAL 2
npm run dev
IMPORTANT
DO NOT refresh before restarting backend.

Old websocket process may still be alive forwarding garbage text like a possessed fax machine.

