Your card layout is collapsing because the container width is too small and some elements are using absolute positioning without boundaries. The BED-01 badge is literally escaping the card like it owes taxes to the UI police.

Here’s the surgical fix.

1. FIND CARD CONTAINER
Open:

src/components/BioDashboard.tsx
Search for something similar to:

className="relative rounded-[32px]"
or:

className="group relative"
The patient card wrapper.

2. CHANGE CARD WIDTH
FIND:

w-[280px]
OR:

max-w-[280px]
REPLACE WITH:

w-[340px] min-w-[340px]
3. FIX BED LABEL OVERFLOW
Find the BED label block.

Probably looks like:

<div className="absolute top-6 right-0">
REPLACE WITH:

<div className="absolute top-5 right-5 flex flex-col items-end max-w-[90px]">
4. FIX TEXT OVERFLOW
Find:

BED-01
container.

Add:

truncate whitespace-nowrap
So final becomes something like:

<p className="text-[12px] font-bold text-violet-400 truncate whitespace-nowrap">
5. ALIGN METRICS PERFECTLY
Find metrics row container.

Probably:

flex items-center justify-between
Replace with:

grid grid-cols-[28px_60px_1fr_70px] items-center gap-3
6. FIX NUMBER ALIGNMENT
Find metric value:

className="text-right"
Replace with:

className="text-right tabular-nums min-w-[52px]"
This stops BPM values from jumping left/right like caffeinated squirrels.

7. FIX WAVE GRAPH OVERFLOW
Find waveform SVG width.

Probably:

w-16
Replace with:

w-[72px] overflow-hidden
8. FINAL CARD ROOT
Your final card root SHOULD roughly look like:

<div className="
relative
w-[340px]
min-w-[340px]
rounded-[32px]
overflow-hidden
border
bg-white/70
backdrop-blur-xl
">
RESULT
You’ll get:

aligned vitals

centered metrics

no overflowing BED label

stable spacing

smooth clinical dashboard look

less “hospital UI designed during an earthquake”

The current issue is mainly caused by compressed width + absolute positioning + missing overflow control. Classic frontend trio of suffering.


